I haven't got any scroll of genocide. But mainly, ranged attacks is one of
the key factors of success in Nethack. Spending genocide is like breaking
a fly on the wheel. WRT genocide, if I have scrolls, I usually just apply
those to 'L' and 'h', and (in case of a single genocide offer) minotauri.
In the given game I was playing a dwarf, so I'd have needed two uncursed
scrolls for erasing MF/MMF. Missile weapons are very convenient to weaken
any approaching monster before you start meleeing them, or if you want to
avoid melee for monster-specific reasons. Interestingly those +5 knifes
had been very effective, even against tougher monsters. In the late game
I used, depending on the circumstances, the Greyswandir for melee, spell
of magic missile for a row of tougher monsters, and the knifes for single
monsters where I wanted to avoid contact.

